# CLAUDE.md

## Project overview

{{name}} (`{{id}}`) is an Obsidian plugin. `src/main.ts` is the entry;
`manifest.json` + `versions.json` describe the release; `main.js` and
`styles.css` are build artifacts (never edit or commit them).

**Architecture, services (EventBus/NoticeService/ModalService), boundaries,
and the add-a-feature checklist live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — read it
before structural changes.**

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev              # watch build; deploys into $OBSIDIAN_VAULT (hot reload)
npm run build            # production bundle (main.js + styles.css)
npm run test             # Vitest (jsdom; `obsidian` aliased to tests/__mocks__/obsidian.ts)
npm run test:coverage    # coverage with rise-only floors
npm run typecheck        # {{typecheckTool}} --noEmit
npm run lint             # eslint (obsidianmd + type-aware rules, all-error)
npm run format           # prettier --write
npm run check:loc        # per-file LOC ratchet
npm run check:css        # CSS !important ratchet (run with -- --update to re-baseline)
npm run check:quality    # fallow metric ratchet (run with ./coverage absent)
npm run check:artifacts  # post-build artifact smoke (run after npm run build)
```

## Development notes

- **Obsidian-native first**: build DOM with `createEl`/`createDiv`/`createSpan`/
  `setText`/`.empty()`; render markdown through `MarkdownRenderer`. Raw HTML
  sinks (`innerHTML`/`outerHTML`/`insertAdjacentHTML`) are lint-banned (XSS).
- No `console.*` in production code (lint-enforced); UI copy is sentence case.
- User feedback goes through `plugin.notices` / `plugin.modals` — raw
  `new Notice()` outside NoticeService is lint-banned.
- Register commands via `plugin.commands` in `src/commands.ts`
  (`addSimple`/`addChecked`/`addEditor`); keep `main.ts` orchestration-only.
- {{mobileLine}}
- {{vueLine}}
- Style with Obsidian CSS variables in `src/styles.css`; avoid `!important`
  (ratcheted by `check:css`).
- **TDD workflow**: for new behavior or bug fixes, write the failing test first
  under `tests/`, make it pass, then refactor.
- Ratchets (`check:loc`, `check:css`, `check:quality`, coverage floors) may
  improve but never regress; lock improvements in with each gate's `--update`
  in the same PR.
- Run `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test && npm run build && npm run check:artifacts`
  before pushing.

## Release flow

`npm version patch|minor|major` syncs `manifest.json` and `versions.json` via
`scripts/sync-version.mjs`; `git push --follow-tags` triggers the release
workflow, which attaches `main.js`, `manifest.json`, and `styles.css`.
